External programs

External providers, model runners, CLIs and optional memory services are not
bundled by the native build scripts. Installing or invoking them separately
does not transfer their licenses to Hyakki's source. Their own distributions
and licenses apply. No Ryoku Account, Ember subscription or third-party
provider account is required for local or user-supplied-model workflows.

Corresponding source

A binary distributor must provide the corresponding source, dependency
sources, license grants and build instructions required by the applicable
licenses. release/source-dist.sh creates a contained source archive from
the direct module, canonical shared Lithic/i18n sources and retained legal metadata.
It does not include the research artifacts, assessment copies or installed
programs. See release/docs/native-distribution.md and release/docs/licensing.md.

