Voice and dictation

Oni's voice loop and dictation bundle no speech engine, model, voice or
recording. They run separately installed programs and use models that are
downloaded only after the user agrees, each pinned by size and SHA-256.
release/docs/oni-licensing.md lists every component with its license, source and
delivery.

- whisper.cpp's whisper-server, with ggml (MIT, the ggml authors,
  https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp), is an external program.
- OpenAI Whisper base.en and large-v3-turbo GGML weights (MIT, OpenAI,
  https://github.com/openai/whisper) and Silero VAD v6.2.0 (MIT, Silero Team,
  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad) are optional downloads.
- ryoku-dictate, Ryoku's dictation program (GPL-3.0-or-later), built on
  transcribe.cpp (MIT, https://github.com/handy-computer/transcribe.cpp) and
  ggml, is used only when it is installed.
- eSpeak NG (GPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng) is
  the default voice. It runs as a separate program; none of its code or data
  is shipped.
- Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0, https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M) with
  unmodified espeak-ng-data (GPL-3.0-or-later) is an optional, removable
  voice pack. It is rendered by sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), an optional external program.
  Hyakki neither bundles nor downloads the pack.
- wtype (MIT, https://github.com/atx/wtype), PipeWire's pw-cat (MIT) and
  PulseAudio's parec, paplay and pactl (LGPL-2.1-or-later) are external
  programs.
- The LibriSpeech ASR corpus (CC BY 4.0, Panayotov et al.,
  https://www.openslr.org/12/) was used only in a private speech benchmark
  and is not distributed.

NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2 (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2)
and Parakeet TDT_CTC 110M (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt_ctc-110m)
are by NVIDIA and licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International license (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
The GGUF files Hyakki can download were converted by handy-computer for
transcribe.cpp (https://huggingface.co/handy-computer/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-gguf,
from NVIDIA's commit 1b149a3;
https://huggingface.co/handy-computer/parakeet-tdt_ctc-110m-gguf, from commit
